Empty on purpose, and tracked on purpose.

main.css names this directory in an @source, and tools/check-sources.mjs fails
the build when a named source path stops existing — so an empty, UNTRACKED
directory is a fresh-clone failure waiting to happen. Git cannot track an empty
directory; this file is what makes the path survive a clone.

It exists because hand-authored page bodies are registered as block patterns
when they need to live in the database: Tailwind does not scan the database, so
a utility class used only inside imported post_content would be missing from
the build with no error anywhere. Patterns are in a scanned directory, and the
importer inserts pattern references rather than expanded HTML.

Today the page bodies are PHP template parts in parts/pages/, so this is empty.
